    "result_text": "The full build passes. Both acceptance tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `ownerSegment` on the owner response, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n\n1. **`OwnerSegments.java`** (new util) \u2014 `segmentFor(owner)` computes the segment:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevels.cappedLevelFor(owner) >= 3` (the same effective level exposed as `membershipLevel`), otherwise `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when `Localities.localityFor(owner)` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD, i.e. not `UNKNOWN`), otherwise `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` wiring `ownerSegment` to `OwnerSegments.segmentFor(owner)`, matching the existing derived-field pattern (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, etc.).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nTests: `coreSegmentForKnownRegion` (Sydney/NSW \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`) and `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` (random city \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) both pass; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
